# One line ending in the repository, whatever the editor on this machine does.
#
# Why this file exists: an editor rewrote 273 files with CRLF in a single pass,
# which git reported as every line of every file having changed. A diff that
# large is a diff nobody reads, and the seven files with real changes in them
# were invisible inside it. Normalising on `git add` makes that class of churn
# impossible rather than merely discouraged.
#
# `eol=lf` on checkout too: the fetchers mirror upstream CSV and TSV that
# arrive with CRLF, the parsers strip `\r` deliberately, and the committed
# mirror is LF. Leaving checkout platform-dependent would make those mirrors
# diff against themselves on Windows for the rest of the project's life.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary by extension, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Kept out of `git archive`, and so out of the tarball a release archives
# under a DOI. `.claude/` is this machine's agent tooling (a launch config),
# not part of the dataset or the site. `.gstack/` stays in: test comments cite
# the QA reports it holds.
.claude/ export-ignore
